**__Concept__:**

**Velocity ratio: **It is defined as the ratio of distance covered by effort force to the distance covered by load and is given as;

V.R.=(Distancespace movespace byspace effortspace force)/(Distancespace movespace byspace load)

**Efficiency: **It is defined as the ratio of mechanical advantage to the velocity ratio and is given as;

<span class="math-tex"

The ratio of RMS value to the average value is known as the form factor.

Form factor = frac{{rms value}}{{average value}}

**__Important Point__:**

The ratio of the maximum value (peak value) to RMS value is known as the peak factor or crest factor.

Peak factor = frac{{maximum value}}{{rms value}}
